    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 **70 tests, 0 failures, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `riskFlag` rule for the `POST /api/owners` \u2192 `GET /api/owners/{id}` endpoint. The flag is `true` when any of the three conditions hold, otherwise `false`:\n\n1. **Possible duplicate** \u2014 the owner's stored `possibleDuplicate` is true (already computed at creation via the soundex-lastName + postcode soft-match).\n2. **Disposable-adjacent email domain** \u2014 any dot-separated label of the email's domain matches a known disposable-mailbox provider (`mailinator`, `tempmail`, `guerrillamail`). This deliberately catches hosts that slip past the existing hard blocklist (which only rejects the exact domains like `mailinator.com` at create time) as subdomains (`inbox.mailinator.com`) or alternate TLDs (`tempmail.io`).\n3. **Over soft capacity** \u2014 the owner's stored `capacityWarning` is true (city held 40\u201349 owners at creation, the soft-capacity band below the hard limit of 50).\n\nChanges:\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `riskFlag` boolean to the `Owner` schema (regenerates `OwnerDto` with getter/setter).\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added `emailDomainDisposableAdjacent(...)` and the combining `riskFlag(Owner)` static helper, reusing the existing stored flags.\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` expression deriving `riskFlag` from the owner, consistent with the other derived fields.\n\nNote: since the concept isn't stored on the entity, I derived `riskFlag` at mapping time from existing stored fields (`possibleDuplicate`, `capacityWarning`) plus the email \u2014 no schema/DB migration needed. The one thing I had to interpret was \"disposable-adjacent\" (the spec text in the test Javadoc was truncated); I read it as the provider-label match described above, which is the natural fit given exact disposable domains are already rejected before an owner can be fetched.",
